# The committed API contracts are evidence about a service rather than source
# code, so git must not rewrite a byte of them.
#
# This machine has core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites line endings on checkout.
# That is harmless for code and fatal for a document whose whole value is that
# it is byte-identical to what the service published: `docs/api/README.md`
# records a SHA-256 for each one so anyone can refetch and verify, and a hash
# computed over a CRLF working copy matches neither the upstream file nor the
# same checkout on Linux. It was already wrong once, quietly, before anyone
# thought to check.
#
# `-text` turns every conversion off, so what is committed, what is checked out,
# and what curl returns are the same bytes on every platform.

docs/api/** -text
desktop-skill/scripts/meturgaman/data/api/** -text
